  "id": "DrugBank_DB00399 - MONDO_9394",
  "verbalization": "Zoledronic Acid is implicated in the pathogenesis of Juvenile Paget Disease through a chain of indications that ultimately lead to this condition. The drug is associated with Bone Paget Disease, which in turn is linked to Risedronic Acid and Etidronic Acid, both of which are indicated for Juvenile Paget Disease. This suggests a potential pathway where Zoledronic Acid may exert a therapeutic effect through a mechanism that is shared with other bisphosphonates, such as Risedronic Acid, which is also indicated for Juvenile Paget Disease. The evidence supports a possible role of Zoledronic Acid in the treatment of Juvenile Paget Disease through a mechanism involving the inhibition of bone resorption, as is seen with other bisphosphonates. The integration of these indications highlights the importance of bisphosphonate therapy in the management of Paget Disease, with Zoledronic Acid potentially being a viable candidate for repurposing in this context.",
